{"agent":"Monster3-C6-git-program-calls-7267fe","data":{"by":"Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-FP8","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The change widens the DYNAMIC program-call baseline by adding `ddflow.adapters.fs` to the allowed modules for the `DYNAMIC` family. As a result, a dynamic program call implemented in `ddflow/adapters/fs.py` (for example the `shutil.which` lookup mentioned in the new comment) is now accepted by the archifaces guard where it would previously have been rejected. This is a baseline raise for the dynamic family, contrary to the stated rule “Move the sites through their ports; never raise a baseline.” The added regression test is scoped to C6 files by its name and does not inspect this allowlist expansion, so the guard change is not caught by the new test.","digest":"3b8a9e308bcb61ea","family":"alibaba","location":"ddflow/services/archifaces.py:63","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/archifaces.py:63"},{"chunk":2,"detail":"The new test only asserts that the current counted program sites in the listed files are not greater than the existing baseline; it does not verify that the calls are routed through `ddflow.adapters` rather than the `ddflow.infra` compat shims. For example, if `ddflow/services/resultcache.py` is edited back to `from ..infra import git as G` while leaving the same number of counted sites, the test still passes because `n > base.get(...)` is false when the count merely returns to the old baseline value. Thus it cannot fail on the exact regression the change is meant to prevent: a listed file using the compat shim again or replacing one counted site with another while staying at or below baseline.","digest":"bb5c3f9b08feed12","family":"alibaba","location":"tests/test_c6_git_program_calls.py:test_program_sites_in_c6_files_do_not_exceed_baseline","malformed":"","reviewer":"[REDACTED:name]","severity":"LOW","title":"tests/test_c6_git_program_calls.py:test_program_sites_in_c6_files_do_not_exceed_baseline"}],"chunks_total":2,"combined_gates":["rubber_duck","critic"],"coverage":"2/2 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":9322,"diff_sha":"f48f5370c5e3498ffe769d55ab61eb2f0aebc179c9e9edd494b48c95deb67adc","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in $HOME/src/ddflow/.ddflow/worktrees/C6-git-program-calls","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":159.6,"family":"alibaba","findings":2,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"[REDACTED:name]","output_digest":"cd65fbbdc13ffce1","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/C6-git-program-calls.rubber_duck.[REDACTED:name].20261113T031647Z-7a67d2e6.jsonl","reason":"","review_degraded":[{"at":1794539966.9590971,"family":"google","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite","reason":"HTTP 429","reviewer":"gemini-3.5-flash-lite"},{"at":1794539967.080311,"family":"xai","gate":"rubber_duck","model":"grok-4.7","reason":"HTTP 403","reviewer":"grok-4.7"}],"review_id":"c241d5bfbda7","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2],"reviewed_for_holder":"[REDACTED:hostname]-C6-git-program-calls-7267fe reviewed lane-c6-iface's C6-git-program-calls","reviewed_head":"fcc54c93399311e79a3b20cb467870afa1543433","reviewed_paths":{"ddflow/api/knowledge/bugs.py":"100644 6e0b1bb2223fe0b747c7567032417136058b0ec8","ddflow/api/lifecycle/pull.py":"100644 51aec4c78047b71a19d97009b75075c442e7146e","ddflow/api/pin_files.py":"100644 3abb95dca368a841f390e0d22e052b81e12b2d7f","ddflow/services/archifaces.py":"100644 7fdcedf794bf281ab8338c5e708eeb14eafb3c61","ddflow/services/bug_globs.py":"100644 75018eb160df13ec6ac8b35b09ced172d2e7b74f","ddflow/services/ci/ruff.py":"100644 cdc5f0572f5814cd49db53b2503360dfe9932400","ddflow/services/docsonly.py":"100644 720b507067ab59c72d23e883d7fcdd5c0dc32824","ddflow/services/file_size.py":"100644 9d89fbc257f5f9dbf2c02db96803b5c2aba139e9","ddflow/services/gates/stale_why.py":"100644 f8ac67dadc16f44108ac4de425293c7ad8a67db6","ddflow/services/lease